Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.30,0:00:18.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had my girlfriend \Nbake some apple pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.86,0:00:19.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Want some?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.18,0:00:32.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.52,0:00:34.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.38,0:00:36.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this is that which is forbidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.13,0:00:40.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I may not know alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.21,0:00:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I do know one thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.81,0:00:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who commit \Nthat which is forbidden...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.40,0:00:49.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.08,0:00:50.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I haven't done a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.82,0:00:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you were planning to try?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.50,0:00:55.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So many died—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.32,0:00:57.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, I killed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.49,0:00:58.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was war.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.39,0:01:01.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You weren't there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.82,0:01:05.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, right. If you couldn't stand \Ngoing to war and killing the enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.96,0:01:09.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you should have chosen \Nduty at the rear, like I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.16,0:01:10.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By becoming a State Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.40,0:01:15.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then calling even some of \Nthose people back to this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.04,0:01:16.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,did you think it would save you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.89,0:01:18.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.71,0:01:22.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is performing the forbidden so straightforward
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.77,0:01:24.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you can just cram for it \Nto be able to pull it off?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.75,0:01:29.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or did you just want to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.79,0:01:32.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's the case, there are easier ways to go about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.93,0:01:39.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As it turns out, I was unable to attempt it, \Nout of fear for my own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.82,0:01:41.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course you couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.13,0:01:43.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's just the kind of person I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.68,0:01:45.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's true about anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.88,0:01:50.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, there is a better way to use the life I have than this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.84,0:01:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maes,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.01,0:01:54.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've made up my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.97,0:01:58.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me more, Roy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.69,0:02:00.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.68,0:02:02.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Lt. Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.93,0:02:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay. I'll wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.46,0:02:11.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.30,0:02:15.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You seem to be investigating \Nthe higher levels of the military, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.90,0:02:19.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, in regards to the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.88,0:02:21.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Regarding that matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.40,0:02:25.09,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I took charge of it personally and concluded it's possible that Brig. Gen. Basque Grand
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.09,0:02:32.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,teamed up with Ishbalan radicals in conducting seditious research.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.07,0:02:34.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you dissatisfied with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.38,0:02:37.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I, uh... Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.67,0:02:41.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, is this about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.30,0:02:43.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. It can be surmised that within the military,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.70,0:02:46.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there was experimentation with creating Philosopher's Stones
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.14,0:02:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that there were various \Nillegal actions taken to that end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.96,0:02:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And it was not all carried out \Nat Brig. Gen. Grand's discretion.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.30,0:02:54.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the very least,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.67,0:02:57.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this also falls upon the succession of superior officers over Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.88,0:03:00.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's possible that these \Npersons were complicit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.36,0:03:04.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major generals, \Nbrigadier generals, colonels...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.91,0:03:06.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Involved in something like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.86,0:03:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. In just the last year, each one has either died or gone missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.54,0:03:16.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, when you consider that \Nthe 5th Laboratory was still operating
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.38,0:03:19.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that just the other day, \NIshbalan refugees were attacked
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.23,0:03:24.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,by someone within the military who employed mercenaries...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.33,0:03:27.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying that even now, \Nsome power within the military
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.45,0:03:30.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is attempting to create a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.05,0:03:35.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If something like that \Never came to light,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.03,0:03:37.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the military would lose its authority!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.39,0:03:42.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm joking! Follow through on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.36,0:03:47.75,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,After all, someone has been conducting prohibited, top-secret human experimentation
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.75,0:03:51.30,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,and then using assassins who call themselves homunculi to wipe out the evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.30,0:03:53.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot overlook such an outrage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.06,0:03:55.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will purge this corruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.20,0:03:57.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.93,0:03:59.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As such, Führer...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.36,0:04:01.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm, Doctor Marcoh, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.83,0:04:05.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to question him for information again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.13,0:04:06.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Juliet...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.87,0:04:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will ask that he be brought to Central immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.95,0:04:13.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, she's the only one who knows where Marcoh is hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.27,0:04:18.46,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It's a precaution to prevent me from revealing anything, even if tortured by the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.40,0:04:21.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well, if you please...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.22,0:04:24.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,uh... Douglas-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.28,0:04:27.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will purge this corruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.04,0:04:32.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.78,0:04:37.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.05,0:04:42.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.79,0:04:48.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.61,0:06:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.82,0:06:27.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this means that all the bigwigs who are connected with the 5th Laboratory
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.99,0:06:30.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,either die or turn up missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.93,0:06:34.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And there weren't any criminals on the list who had the Uroboros mark on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.18,0:06:37.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds like they're talking about some scary stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.96,0:06:41.92,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I don't want to stick my nose into any more trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.22,0:06:47.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, there should still be scientists who worked under Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.67,0:06:51.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we could find some of them...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.00,0:06:53.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, leave that to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.06,0:06:55.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.28,0:06:58.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like it doesn't \Nreally matter anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.18,0:07:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you guys talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.03,0:07:02.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.26,0:07:06.32,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,we've had enough of the Philosopher's Stone and homunculi and other dicey stuff like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.32,0:07:10.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that maybe, it would be smarter to look for a different method.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.41,0:07:12.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That would definitely be smarter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.55,0:07:15.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if you could find it that simply, there wouldn't be any sport in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.58,0:07:19.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There {\i1}is{\i0} one person who might know something about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.05,0:07:20.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.05,0:07:23.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She lives to the south, \Nin a place called Dublith.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.72,0:07:25.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We plan on paying her a visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.72,0:07:27.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric brothers...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.26,0:07:30.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here, just one stop before Dublith!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.34,0:07:32.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is there something there?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.54,0:07:35.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the holy land of \NAutomail mechanics, Rush Valley!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.47,0:07:37.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've always wanted to go there!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.43,0:07:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take me with you! Take me with you! Take me with you! Take me with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.98,0:07:41.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go there by yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.50,0:07:43.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But who's going to pay \Nmy traveling expenses?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.35,0:07:44.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're trying to mooch off of us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.82,0:07:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay, isn't it? \NIt's on the way, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.31,0:07:49.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the use?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.00,0:07:50.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.22,0:07:56.42,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,So those two have finally decided not to get involved in any more dangerous business, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.42,0:07:59.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They must have realized how hard it was for us to guard them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.76,0:08:00.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh, uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.76,0:08:03.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that were the case, \Nwhat fun would that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.90,0:08:08.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is all to keep us from \Nbecoming the next victims.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.09,0:08:12.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pretty sharp for a kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.82,0:08:36.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not going to Dublith?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.82,0:08:39.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we {\i1}are{\i0} going as far as Rush Valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.72,0:08:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, okay. \NBut why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.71,0:08:44.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Weren't you going to ask your teacher
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.37,0:08:46.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,about other methods besides the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.58,0:08:48.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we did that, we'd be killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.91,0:08:51.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Killed?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.74,0:08:57.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We never told our teacher about becoming State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.56,0:09:00.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not to mention that if it got out that \Nwe had performed human transmutation...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.57,0:09:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to live a little bit longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.90,0:09:07.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would at least like to have fallen in love, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.14,0:09:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And even if that weren't the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.19,0:09:15.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get the feeling we shouldn't ask our teacher about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.07,0:09:17.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what are you going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.77,0:09:22.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a large-scale Ishbalan camp in the mountains to the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.49,0:09:25.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm guessing that Scar and \Nthe others are headed there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.26,0:09:28.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going after Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.21,0:09:31.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's said that a Philosopher's Stone was once created at Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.78,0:09:36.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But since they never had alchemy introduced to them in the first place,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.19,0:09:40.68,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,we think it might be possible that they \Ncreated it in a completely different manner.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.93,0:09:44.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to pound on him \Nand make him tell us the secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.92,0:09:50.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, Brother, he really isn't that bad a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.18,0:09:52.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.08,0:09:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he uses alchemy to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.48,0:09:56.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't let him \Nget away with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.21,0:10:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.76,0:10:29.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.52,0:10:32.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?! You are not of the people of Ishbal, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.86,0:10:34.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, how rude of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.14,0:10:37.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've failed to introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.40,0:10:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the State Alchemist in charge of exterminating this region.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.47,0:10:56.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got a visitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.55,0:11:01.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.28,0:11:06.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so glad you are safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.00,0:11:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm impressed that \Nyou survived as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.67,0:11:10.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where have you been up to now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.02,0:11:14.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are a certain number of us \Nliving in the mountains to the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.48,0:11:18.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were planning on \Nvisiting there ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.73,0:11:23.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our countrymen who were in Central were coming to meet us,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.04,0:11:25.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,traveling so as not to catch the military's attention,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.09,0:11:29.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when along the way, \Nthey heard stories about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.60,0:11:32.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In these last three years,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.46,0:11:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they say you've been going around killing State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.13,0:11:41.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was State Alchemists who burned down our villages.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.79,0:11:43.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can understand your \Nfeelings of resentment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.89,0:11:45.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's true!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.39,0:11:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These guys are Ishbalans, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.80,0:11:56.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure it's safe to be \Nhanging around in a place like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.40,0:12:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aren't you guys supposed to be living in the designated camps?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.07,0:12:11.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what you are doing is taking out \Nyour anger in sworn vengeance, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.11,0:12:15.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Vengeance only sows the seeds of renewed vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.05,0:12:21.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the ancient words of Ishbala, it says:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.77,0:12:24.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Those who receive pain can still sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.16,0:12:29.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Those who give pain cannot sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.01,0:13:03.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That arm of yours...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.25,0:13:06.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that your brother's arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.68,0:13:15.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you report to me that the \NElric brothers had been put in a hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.44,0:13:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Didn't I mention that? Well, it's no big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.50,0:13:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind them,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.50,0:13:21.18,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,No big deal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.18,0:13:25.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it sounds like your posting to Central is going to be formally settled on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.25,0:13:26.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry up and make yourself important
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.83,0:13:28.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you can make things easier for the rest of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.58,0:13:29.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And find yourself a wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.41,0:13:31.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be gentle with the telephone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.99,0:13:33.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant, get us a train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.30,0:13:36.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To Central?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.62,0:13:38.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something is going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.68,0:13:43.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mustang-san is just \Nworried about those two.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.68,0:13:46.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no need to \Nworry him unnecessarily,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.84,0:13:49.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,nor does he need to know \Nabout any of the nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.35,0:13:54.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For one thing, it's possible that our phones are being tapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.70,0:13:57.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I still have \Nthings to look into.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.50,0:13:59.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.55,0:14:03.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa still has lots of work to do. \NI'll be back later.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.57,0:14:09.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bring me the materials \Non the Liore riots!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.11,0:14:09.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.86,0:14:13.37,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Where are the diagrams of the \Ntransmutation circles from the 5th Laboratory?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.37,0:14:15.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The budget from the first year of the Ishbal Rebellion!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.60,0:14:21.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I going to get \Novertime pay for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.34,0:14:23.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll give you a picture of Elicia!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.18,0:14:33.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal... Liore... Mugear's mines...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.08,0:14:36.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once they got near a Philosopher's Stone, \Nthey were destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.95,0:14:38.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strange, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.62,0:14:42.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they're driving people to \Ncreate a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.79,0:14:44.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why would they spread stories around
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.41,0:14:47.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that destruction befalls those who seek the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.19,0:14:50.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it to get rid of all the evidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.51,0:14:52.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No... It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.08,0:14:55.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just the opposite, could it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.28,0:14:57.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposing everything was reversed...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.80,0:15:03.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on... The unit that caused \Nthe outbreak of war in Ishbal was...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.54,0:15:06.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...Douglas? Where have \NI heard that name before?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.04,0:15:08.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, there's a phone call \Nfrom the Führer's secretary.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.34,0:15:13.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, Doctor Marcoh has arrived in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.91,0:15:15.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is waiting at the hotel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.61,0:15:18.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much. \NI will go see him right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.26,0:15:24.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Douglas... Juliet...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.34,0:15:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka! Put all of these materials back where you found them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.10,0:15:34.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once that's done, you can go home! \NAlso, you're fired!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.45,0:15:35.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't ever come around here again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.79,0:15:41.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to put you \Nthrough all this trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.33,0:15:44.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ms. Secretary... Douglas-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.30,0:15:46.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you know much \Nabout the Ishbalan War?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.85,0:15:49.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I have always had desk jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.81,0:15:51.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So have I, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.83,0:15:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been looking into \Nsome things lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.70,0:15:57.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know that the reason the rebellion broke out
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.78,0:16:03.31,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,was that one of the soldiers stationed there recklessly shot and killed an Ishbalan child?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.31,0:16:07.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That soldier's name, \Nit turns out, was Juliet Douglas.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.50,0:16:10.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a common name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.72,0:16:14.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where it gets interesting. The soldier with that name
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.39,0:16:18.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was supposed to have died two years before the Ishbal Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.43,0:16:19.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is odd.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.92,0:16:22.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's one other "odd" thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.21,0:16:25.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Douglas was dead before then.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.00,0:16:29.21,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,And yet the muster roll for this person \Nnamed Juliet Douglas was never withdrawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.51,0:16:32.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the contrary, \Nover the last two years,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.64,0:16:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the soldier with that name \Nhas been suddenly promoted.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.60,0:16:40.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now, she has been promoted to the Führer's Ministerial Secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.83,0:16:44.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.48,0:16:46.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you at Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.62,0:16:51.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or did you just use Douglas's \Nregistration to get into the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.92,0:16:53.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Doctor is waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.18,0:16:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that even Marcoh \Nbehind that door?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.04,0:17:03.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.00,0:17:05.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or perhaps, "farewell" \Nmight be more appropriate.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.74,0:17:09.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a cool tattoo \Nyou've got there, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.21,0:17:13.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.64,0:17:23.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was unexpectedly skillful, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.41,0:17:26.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth, make sure to let everyone know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.98,0:17:33.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Ross, \Nthey're right next to the Führer!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.55,0:17:37.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The enemy has fully infiltrated the military. Their purpose...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.24,0:17:40.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is not to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.21,0:17:42.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.80,0:17:44.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.18,0:17:45.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.12,0:17:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, dammit...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.52,0:17:51.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, what a pain...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.86,0:17:55.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? He's not there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.88,0:17:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He left for Central with Lieutenant Hawkeye.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.58,0:18:00.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.92,0:18:02.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With this information,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.76,0:18:05.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he had a chance to rise \Nright to the top!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.28,0:18:07.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any event, we should get to someplace safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.73,0:18:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right. It's not as though \NI've got nothing left to hang onto.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.13,0:18:14.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you \Ntell me all about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.24,0:18:19.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lieutenant has a mole under one of her eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.30,0:18:21.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.23,0:18:23.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I must have gotten careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.16,0:18:31.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.32,0:18:43.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.07,0:18:46.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have a wife and daughter waiting for me at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.14,0:18:54.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a pretty good act, \Nwasn't it, Lt. Colonel Hughes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.89,0:19:11.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to become the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.33,0:19:15.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to change \Nthe way this country runs.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.52,0:19:18.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the only thing I can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.51,0:19:24.01,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Then you'll need someone who \Nunderstands you and can support you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.86,0:19:29.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone underneath you, who can push you upward.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.36,0:20:24.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, why? Why are they burying Papa?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.87,0:20:29.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Why are those men burying Papa?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.81,0:20:30.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.98,0:20:33.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elicia...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.00,0:20:34.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want them to.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.53,0:20:35.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want them to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.81,0:20:39.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they do that, then Papa \Ncan't do his work anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.88,0:20:41.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, stop them!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.00,0:20:43.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elicia...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.47,0:20:46.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa said he still had \Na lot of work to do!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.90,0:20:48.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want them to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.42,0:20:51.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't bury him! Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.94,0:20:54.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa! Papa!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.23,0:21:13.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Killed in the line of duty and \Nposthumously promoted two ranks...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.16,0:21:15.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General Hughes, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.91,0:21:20.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I going to do \Nnow that the man who said
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.79,0:21:24.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he would stay beneath me and assist me \Nhas gone above me, you idiot?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.04,0:21:27.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.49,0:21:32.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once, I tried putting together a theory \Non how to perform human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.93,0:21:36.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just now, I was frantically remembering it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.80,0:21:39.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We alchemists are nasty creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.64,0:21:43.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the Elric brothers \Nwere mixed up in this,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.07,0:21:45.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why didn't he report it to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.83,0:21:48.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He didn't have to go \Ncharging into this alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.28,0:21:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Haven't you figured it out yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.62,0:21:55.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Figured what out?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.34,0:21:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When it comes to those brothers,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.18,0:22:01.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel has been known to \Nlose his level-headed judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.32,0:22:05.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, Brigadier General Hughes
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.74,0:22:09.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,took everything concerning \Nthe Elric brothers upon himself,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.79,0:22:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that the Colonel could relax
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.18,0:22:13.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and set his sights above himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.18,0:22:24.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's starting to rain, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.40,0:22:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.38,0:22:42.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if this is like the food that Mom used to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.09,0:22:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hughes-san, his wife, and Elicia-chan were all such fine people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.80,0:22:48.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.74,0:22:53.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel Hughes is a mother hen and a busybody. He bothers me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.13,0:22:55.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He always used to come to joke around with us, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.58,0:22:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every day, he said \Nhe was busy with work,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.40,0:23:00.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but he still always \Ncame by to check on us.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.20,0:23:04.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder why he looked after us \Nas much as he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.69,0:23:06.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.06,0:23:09.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When we get back to Central, make sure you thank him.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.67,0:23:26.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.20,0:23:30.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.24,0:23:32.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.70,0:25:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.45,0:25:32.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 26: "Her Reason"
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.68,0:25:35.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never even thought about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.84,0:25:39.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could there be somebody \Nwho felt that way about me?
